<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polans (western)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Polanie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polans were a West Slavic tribe of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, in the basin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warta">Warta</a> river around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poznan">Poznań</a>. In the 10th century their Piast rulers, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-i">Mieszko I</a>, united the neighbouring tribes into the Polish state, which took its name from them. They are distinct from the East Slavic Polans of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polans-western.jpg" alt="Polans (western)" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pedros.lol · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grody_w_okresie_Mieszka_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
